    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b6a161e2-1efa-5030-b26b-a1a45004731b" activityNameId="9a4a5a0d-1a6d-5802-852a-a20c24abccc2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Railway track</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Railway track
All data is referred to meter*year. Life time of the rail track infrastructure is assumed to be 100 yrs. Inventory for a conventional gravel track bedding. Expenditures due to tunnel construction and bridge construction have been taken into account, according to the share of tunnels and bridges in the Swiss rail network.  All data is referred to a two way track. Allocation between goods and passenger transport is not yet applied;
UUID: 81085e38-b471-33ae-a18f-55686d931f3c
The inventory includes the construction of the rail track (track bedding, substructures, catenary system) as well as the construction of tunnels and bridges. Further components of rail track infrastructure, such as signalling infrastructure, train overtaking stations, sound insulation walls and buildings (stations, service garages) are not included in this study. Also land use is not considered, but accounted for in the maintenance and operation, railway track.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data represents current technologies
Time period: Rail length is based on current statistical data (2000). The material consumption represents a situation in the early 1990ties and a recent high speed track in Germany
Production volume: na
Sampling: national statistics and literature studies 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_81085e38-b471-33ae-a18f-55686d931f3c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
